From 5ae35051e23b0023339e9bc6c743e02e6475104b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:41:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban pacing: start a paced card on a class route
 with room instead of holding it

Pool workers 2026-11-15 10:09Z: the quota pace governor held Anthropic and openai-codex to one running card each
(llm_paced), so ready cards queued for hours, although each worker's routing registry can hold a subscription
route in the same class on a pool with room: Grok on xai-oauth (X Ultra subscription; entitlement checked: hub
xai-oauth pool row -> POST api.x.ai/v1/responses grok-4.7 -> HTTP 200, served grok-4.7), or a governed pool
still behind pace. The governor only knew "start on this route" or "hold"; it never asked whether the card's
class had another route (t_d943a79dd2b3889f).

Five whys: cards queue -> hold() returns True -> every candidate pool of the card's route is ahead of pace ->
a default card's route is one concrete provider (gpt-6-astra/openai-codex, or claude-opus after a wall move)
-> the governor never consulted the class alternates the quota-wall path already uses (alternate_route).

Change:
- kanban_llm_pacing_dispatch._pace_alternate: when every candidate pool holds the card, probe the same
  non-allocating alternate_route the quota-episode/wall path uses, with the holding pools as extra walls.
  Eligibility is the worker's own (billing/capability, subscription-only, funding_verified), unpinned default
  or strong-class routes only; mandatory pins, model/provider overrides and require_model cards still wait.
  A governed target is pace-judged only when the probe names it (no extra usage reads), a target that does not
  serve on this host's live pool (no credential) or shows a quota wall is excluded and the probe retried
  (bounded). Any fault keeps today's hold.
- hold(): with an alternate, the card is not held; the move is offered to the route applier.
  pickup_hold(): a card the local claim would start on an alternate is not held from pickup.
- New kanban_pace_reroute: process-local offer/take handoff (120 s TTL, taken once, bound to the judged
  route) so the governor stays the only reader of pace state (test_only_kanban_dispatch_consults_the_governor
  unchanged). apply_model_tier takes the offer after its own resolution and records the move on run_route:
  tier_reason "<reason>+paced:<paced providers>", provider/model = the alternate.

xai-oauth stays ungoverned: there is no usage endpoint for it (account_usage has no xai branch), so its pool is
never paced; a real rate limit there walls through the existing quota-episode path.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pace_reroute.py (10): RED on main for the three move cases (default card
-> grok when anthropic+codex paced, default codex card -> open anthropic sonnet, pickup), GREEN here; holds kept
for no Grok credential, ineligible/unfunded Grok route, override and require_model pins, probe fault; offer
binding and TTL. All 29 test files importing kanban_llm_pacing_dispatch/kanban_model_tier (756 tests) pass;
scripts/check --base origin/main: 20 checks ok.

Deployment: inert until a host's model_routing registry lists an eligible, funding-verified Grok route and the
host holds an xai-oauth credential (state PRs: relay accepts xai-oauth #3298, then mint + worker routes).
